  "seven_q": {
    "Q0_posture": "This document asserts a structural isomorphism between the Born Rule and the Trinity, claiming it is forced and testable.",
    "Q1_identity": "A formal isomorphism paper (ISO-004) establishing a level-3 structural mapping between quantum measurement and Trinitarian theology.",
    "Q2_domain": "Physics and theology, with strong mathematical and philosophical foundations.",
    "Q3_claim": "The three irreducible operations of the Born Rule (state vector, projection, modulus squared) map exactly to the three Persons of the Trinity (Father, Son, Spirit) in a non-arbitrary, bidirectional, and testable way.",
    "Q4_support": "Six biblical events tested with zero role violations; four separator tests passed (irreducibility, anti-modalism, non-arbitrariness, bidirectionality); seven kill conditions defined.",
    "Q5_dependencies": "Depends on the Born Rule being irreducible to fewer than three operations; depends on Trinitarian theology being irreducible to fewer than three Persons.",
    "Q6_consequences": "If true, physics provides independent evidence for the Trinity; theology provides a deeper understanding of quantum measurement; the mapping forces specific roles for each Person.",
    "Q7_kill": "Seven kill conditions: wrong Born Rule operation, reducibility of Born Rule, non-Trinitarian theology producing same mapping, Spirit not actualizing, Father actively selecting, Son not structuring, any tested event failing."
  },
